<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Connect IQ app: control an Orion Sleep smart mattress topper (oga-fsf). -->
<!--
     type="watch-app" (Device App): still explicitly launched from the Apps
     menu for the actual control flow (turn the bed on/off, set temperature).
     Also supplies a glance (OrionGlanceView, via getGlanceView()) for a
     quick status peek from the widget swipe loop. The installed SDK
     (9.2.0) no longer has a separate "widget" manifest type (see each
     device's compiler.json under the SDK's Devices/ dir: appTypes lists
     "glance" as a capability of watchApp, not a standalone "widget" type),
     so a glance is just an extra view on an ordinary Device App, not a
     type change. The glance does no network I/O (tight update budget); it
     only reads OrionAuth.hasStoredToken(). Selecting it opens the same
     getInitialView() flow a launch from the Apps menu would.

     Targets both watch and Edge device families (multi-family). Screen
     shapes/resolutions differ substantially between them (see compiler.json
     per device under the installed SDK's Devices/ dir) — round ~260-454px
     square watch faces vs. tall rectangular Edge screens — so views must lay
     out from dc.getWidth()/getHeight() at runtime (same approach GarminMerge's
     PRListView already uses) rather than fixed pixel coordinates. Edge devices
     also vary in touch support; input handling should go through
     WatchUi.BehaviorDelegate's onKey/onSelect/onTap so both button-only and
     touch devices work without device-specific branches (again mirroring
     GarminMerge's PRListDelegate).

     Device list below is the full set of watchApp-capable build targets
     (162 ids), generated from the locally installed Connect IQ SDK 9.2.0's
     Devices/*/compiler.json, filtered to devices whose appTypes include
     watchApp — matching this manifest's type="watch-app". Re-verify
     product ids against the current SDK's Devices/ directory periodically
     since Garmin adds/renames devices over time.
-->
